WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.201
An air defense says they were able

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.135
to destroy dozens

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.403
of Russian missiles and drones

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:03.870
that took part

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.271
in an early morning attack.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:06.740
Authorities say the two Ukrainians,

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:07.607
including an 11 year

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.609
old child, were injured by falling debris

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.211
Also today, more attacks

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:11.878
inside Russia,

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.046
according to officials there.

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.714
They say Ukrainian shelling in the border

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.750
region of Belgorod killed two people.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:17.851
And an official in western

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.352
Russia says two drones

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.087
struck fuel facilities.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.022
Now, early this week,

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.323
a drone attack on Moscow left

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:24.724
at least two people injured

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:26.493
and several buildings damaged.

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:28.328
There was a significant turn in a war

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:29.763
that until recently had left Russia

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:32.065
largely untouched.

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:33.299
Today, Vladimir

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:33.733
Putin appeared

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:34.401
to acknowledge

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:35.702
these strikes on his country,

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:36.403
calling them attempts

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:37.437
to destabilize

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:38.972
and, quote, stir up the situation

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.673
within the Russian Federation.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:41.041
Our Fred

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:41.941
Pleitgen joins us

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:42.675
now from Ukraine

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.978
with a look inside the drone war.

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:45.912
Fred, can you just talk about

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.747
how things have changed for Ukrainians

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:48.181
with this now

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:49.482
constant threat of drone strikes

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:52.786
Well, it's certainly changed

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:53.253
a great deal.

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.320
And I think for a lot of people, it's

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.055
really unnerving,

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.689
especially here in the capital, Kiev.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:57.824
Anderson, I can tell you

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.692
there's a lot of nights where people here

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.127
just simply don't get any sleep

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.095
because they live in fear

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.029
the entire time.

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:05.065
And the way that these drone attacks work

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:06.166
is they usually have swarms

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:07.333
of those charged drones

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.701
as Iranian made drones

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.770
coming towards the Ukrainian capital.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.806
You hear the engines hover above you

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.140
and you hear the Ukrainians

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.442
trying to take them down.

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:16.142
But of course,

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:16.776
what's happening

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:17.977
now is that the Ukrainians

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:18.945
are fighting back.

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:20.380
They've launched their own

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.881
mass live drone program.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.017
It's a huge priority for the Ukrainians

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.118
with which they can now

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:26.453
project power deep,

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:28.621
not only into Russian held territory,

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.757
but into Russian territory as well.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:31.458
Here's what we're learning.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.060
Can this fly into Russia?

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:34.727
Yes.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.162
Valery Breivik's

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:36.696
company

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.031
makes combat drones

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:40.767
for Ukrainian frontline troops

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.001
and they allowed us to film

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.170
test flights at a secret location.

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:47.273
He says reaching Moscow is not a problem.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.608
We have bigger draw

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:52.479
for and 700 kilometers with war

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:56.516
has had 20 kilograms and that could fly

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.784
almost almost overnight.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:58.451
Yes,

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.588
While Ukraine denies direct involvement

00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:03.389
in the recent Moscow drone attack,

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.725
Kiev has drastically expanded

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.127
its use of drones

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.695
for everything from surveillance

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:09.562
to directly

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:13.099
bombing Russian ground troops.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:16.302
Cheap, easy to use and lethal UAV.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:17.770
Considered toys

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.973
are now vital to Kiev's war effort

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.009
The Ukrainians say for them,

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:25.378
drones are the big equalizer in this war.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:25.678
They say

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:26.913
the Russians have more tanks,

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.414
more artillery and more planes.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.382
But the Ukrainians

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.584
have the creativity of their population.

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.720
This is a drone competition

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.522
organized by Ukraine's government,

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:38.191
with simulated attacks on ground targets

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.360
chasing fixed

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.861
wing drones

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.031
and even drone

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.533
dogfights.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:50.837
We were granted

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.805
exclusive access on the condition

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.774
we don't reveal the location.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.843
It's like a start up fair for SPV.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.511
Your first person view,

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.280
drones, small UAV

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.314
that can drop mortars

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:02.582
and grenades

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:05.285
flown by pilots wearing VR goggles

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.886
from a makeshift trench

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:10.290
to simulate the battlefield.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:10.690
So

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:12.125
for us,

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:14.227
our drones are very easy to use,

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.728
especially if the pilot has flown

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:16.996
similar drones

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.865
I think they will intuitively understand

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:20.366
how they work.

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.101
The stakes are immense.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.169
A general involved

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:24.737
in drone procurement for Ukraine's

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.039
military tells me

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:26.739
that this could risk

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:27.540
to complaining about.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.042
30 companies in Ukraine

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:31.544
are already mass producing these drones.

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:32.478
And our goal

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:33.479
is to purchase up

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:35.748
to 200,000 by the end of the year.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.684
Their backs up against the wall.

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:38.351
When Russia's

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.453
massive army invaded last year,

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:41.888
the Ukrainians quickly

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.990
realized cheap air power could help

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.825
keep them in the fight.

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:46.960
First, using modified

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.061
consumer drones,

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.896
now with more sophisticated

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:52.065
UAV is developed in Ukraine.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.166
What the government here

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:54.934
calls the Army of Drones

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:55.668
Project

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.237
spearheaded by the Minister

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:58.905
of Digital Transformation.

00:03:58.905 --> 00:03:59.973
So the completion of

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:01.441
this is a technological war,

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:03.343
and it's very important to understand

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:04.978
how technology is developing

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:07.213
and what we as a state can do to increase

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:08.681
the number of drones.

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:10.683
A certain revolution is also taking place

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.752
regarding production scaling the most of

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:13.920
this time.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.121
And while the Ukrainians

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.290
still won't admit direct involvement,

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:18.524
the Russians do admit

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.892
they are concerned

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.995
they might soon see more armed drones

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.463
flying towards Moscow.

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:26.032
It's incredible to see it

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:27.033
up close like that, Fred.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:27.834
Is there any indication

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.168
when we could see these drones

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.670
Ukraine is purchasing, you know,

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.739
above the battlefield in in the fight

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.276
Well, I think it could be very soon.

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:36.442
You know,

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:37.910
some of the drones that we saw there

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.646
at that drone competition,

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:40.913
they've already been on the battlefield,

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.215
but in small quantities.

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:44.417
And I think one of the things, Anderson,

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.752
that we all need to understand

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.220
is that on every battlefield

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.188
here in Ukraine, whether it's Bermuda,

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.690
whether it's in the south,

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:51.691
in the rear echelon

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:52.492
of those battlefields,

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:54.360
you always have a small little shop

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.029
that's developing new drones

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:57.563
and that's trying to improve

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:58.197
some of the drones

00:04:58.197 --> 00:04:59.832
that are already there, for instance,

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.501
to make it impossible for the Russians

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:02.468
to go locate

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:04.037
the person who's operating the drone

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:05.238
or to make it impossible

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:06.472
to hack into those drones.

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.174
So that's already happening all the time.

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.542
Well, the government here tells me is

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:10.176
they want to make it

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:11.544
as quick as possible,

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:13.746
that they find a startup, identify

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:15.381
that that startup could help them

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:16.716
and then scale up production

00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:17.650
as fast as possible

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.585
so we could see some of these drones

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:21.621
on the battlefield very soon Anderson.

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:22.121
It's incredible.

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:23.222
Fred Pleitgen, appreciate it.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:24.791
Perspective now

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:26.392
from CNN military analyst, retired Army

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:27.794
Lieutenant General Mark Hertling.

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:28.194
I mean,

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:29.829
the use of drones is so interesting,

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:30.563
not only in this war,

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.131
but in all future conflicts.

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:33.199
But what do you make of

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:34.634
how drones are being used right now

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.369
in the war in Ukraine?

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:39.539
Well, they're the insertion

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:40.740
of these private sector

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.109
operators is very good, Anderson.

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:44.310
You know,

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.812
these are not that new

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:47.880
drones have been around for a while.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.616
I had back in 2008 when I was in Iraq.

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:53.186
All of our units had small what we called

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:54.387
raven drones,

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:55.922
which were literally hand

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:58.191
launched, would give infantry units

00:05:58.191 --> 00:05:58.758
the opportunity

00:05:58.758 --> 00:06:00.960
to see ahead of them in the battle

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.229
to even look inside buildings at times.

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:06.232
So Ukraine is actually taking this

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:07.700
to a new level.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.235
The drones in the past,

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:10.770
the unmanned aerial systems,

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.338
as we like to call them,

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:15.641
are something that is an advancement

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.009
on the battlefield today.

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:18.044
But I got to tell you

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:21.247
what we've seen in terms of using drones

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:23.349
in Ukraine beyond Reconoce fence,

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:26.018
but to actually drop munitions to

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:29.222
counter electronic warfare.

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:31.190
These are some new opportunities,

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:32.125
I think, in warfare

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:33.126
and is certainly going to change

00:06:33.126 --> 00:06:33.626
the scene.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:35.661
We're learning a lot from Ukraine

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:37.997
and their use of drones.

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.265
So do you think that the U.S.

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:42.301
military is looking at that as something

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:43.469
they may want to incorporate

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:44.771
or figure out how to incorporate

00:06:44.771 --> 00:06:46.506
or explore more?

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:47.640
Oh, we've been looking at it

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:48.941
for a long time, Anderson.

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:49.776
In fact,

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:51.210
at our training centers

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.779
five or six years ago,

00:06:52.779 --> 00:06:55.081
they actually introduced drone swarms.

00:06:55.615 --> 00:06:57.750
We saw those kind of things in the war

00:06:57.984 --> 00:06:59.852
between Armenia and Azerbaijan

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:01.187
just a few years ago

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:02.755
when there were opportunities

00:07:02.755 --> 00:07:04.991
to destroy tanks with drones.

00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:06.092
And in the

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:08.261
in the battle in Nagorno-Karabakh,

00:07:08.261 --> 00:07:10.830
it was an area where surprised

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:11.798
a lot of people,

00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:13.366
Iranians have been using them

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:14.600
for a very long time.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.302
But again, the publication

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:18.137
and the social media aspect of

00:07:18.137 --> 00:07:20.072
what's been happening in Ukraine,

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:22.008
I think it's surprised a lot of people

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:22.742
who don't know that

00:07:22.742 --> 00:07:23.576
drone warfare

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:25.945
is now a part of the modern battlefield.

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:27.180
But this has been going on

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.181
for quite some time.

00:07:28.181 --> 00:07:29.415
But a great report by Fred

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:30.383
Pleitgen just now.

00:07:30.383 --> 00:07:32.852
Yeah, to see the private

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:34.120
sector components. Fascinating.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:35.588
Russia's defense ministry said today

00:07:35.588 --> 00:07:37.089
a group of Chechen special forces

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:37.723
have begun

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:39.559
an offensive in eastern Ukraine.

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:41.461
Obviously, we've heard a

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:42.829
lot about the volunteer forces.

00:07:42.829 --> 00:07:43.729
There were probably Chechens

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:44.864
involved in that as well.

00:07:44.864 --> 00:07:46.132
But there were Chechens

00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:48.434
involved early on in the attempt

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:50.303
to decapitate the leadership

00:07:50.303 --> 00:07:53.773
in Kiev in the first days of this war.

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:55.675
We haven't heard much about them

00:07:55.675 --> 00:07:57.310
over the last year or so.

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:59.011
Do you think that I mean,

00:07:59.011 --> 00:07:59.879
is that significant

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:00.847
that they're announcing

00:08:00.847 --> 00:08:03.149
that there's Chechens now?

00:08:03.216 --> 00:08:05.351
Yeah, I don't believe it is, Anderson.

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:06.452
What we've seen.

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:07.286
Excuse me, is Mr.

00:08:07.286 --> 00:08:08.287
Putin attempting

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:10.389
to get a variety of groups

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:12.091
to do his fighting for him?

00:08:12.091 --> 00:08:14.327
And part of the reason for that is

00:08:14.327 --> 00:08:16.496
there are people who are selling him

00:08:16.496 --> 00:08:17.363
on these groups,

00:08:17.363 --> 00:08:19.866
being capable of conducting operations

00:08:19.866 --> 00:08:21.267
when they're really not

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:22.268
They're used to certain

00:08:22.268 --> 00:08:24.003
kinds of battlefields

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:25.137
destroying things

00:08:25.137 --> 00:08:27.406
like they did in Chechnya, in Syria.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:28.975
Excuse me.

00:08:28.975 --> 00:08:32.245
And they don't take the place of good,

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:34.514
well-trained soldiers who are well-led

00:08:34.547 --> 00:08:35.414
on the battlefield,

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:37.250
under NATO supervision.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:37.650
They're just

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:38.918
a bunch of thugs

00:08:38.918 --> 00:08:41.554
and private military corporations

00:08:41.554 --> 00:08:42.421
Part of it

00:08:42.655 --> 00:08:44.524
seems to be also psychological.

00:08:44.524 --> 00:08:45.925
You know that,

00:08:45.992 --> 00:08:46.659
as you said, that

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:47.960
there's a lots of people in the fight,

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.996
but also that Chechens have a reputation

00:08:49.996 --> 00:08:52.265
of just being thugs and brutal and.

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:55.835
Yeah, just horrific.

00:08:55.835 --> 00:08:56.135
Yeah.

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:58.104
And I'm not sure how to compare them

00:08:58.104 --> 00:08:59.438
to the Wagner group.

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:00.139
And I'm not sure

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:01.807
you can get more thuggish

00:09:01.807 --> 00:09:03.543
than the kind of prisoners that Mr.

00:09:03.543 --> 00:09:05.478
Prigozhin recruited

00:09:05.478 --> 00:09:06.345
in the last phase

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:07.680
of the Battle of Back Moon.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:08.314
But again,

00:09:08.314 --> 00:09:10.883
it's just trying to throw a bunch of

00:09:11.417 --> 00:09:13.152
free floating electrons on

00:09:13.152 --> 00:09:14.287
to the battlefield

00:09:14.287 --> 00:09:16.589
that aren't in very large groups

00:09:16.589 --> 00:09:18.758
or don't have any operational savvy.

00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:20.993
They're just flat out killers. Right.

00:09:20.993 --> 00:09:22.828
But when you don't have the capability

00:09:22.828 --> 00:09:24.363
to conduct operations, either

00:09:24.363 --> 00:09:25.831
offenses or defenses,

00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:27.166
and you're just throwing yourself

00:09:27.166 --> 00:09:29.001
into the fight with a weapon,

00:09:29.001 --> 00:09:30.403
things don't end up doing well.

00:09:30.403 --> 00:09:31.103
And we've seen that

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:31.837
with the Wagner Group.

